Native applications
===============================================================================

`mech build` is the authoritative build command. It accepts exactly one
resident source root or exactly one official `.mecb` file.

~~~sh
mech build app.mec --workspace-root . --out target/mech/app
mech build app.mec --emit bytecode --out target/mech/app.mecb
mech build app.mec --emit plan --workspace-root . --out target/mech/app.build-plan.json
mech build app.mec --emit cargo-project --workspace-root . --out target/mech/app.cargo
~~~

The default emit is `native`, the default profile is `release`, and the
default dependency source is the released registry. Use `--name` to choose a
binary name, `--target` for a Cargo target triple, `--profile debug|release`
for a native profile, and `--out` for the exact artifact path.

`--config <MCFG>` supplies runtime host configuration; `--no-config` disables
discovery. `--workspace-root <PATH>` selects local component paths instead of
the registry. `--offline` is forwarded to generated Cargo operations.
`--keep-project` copies the deterministic generated project beside an emitted
native binary, bytecode file, or plan. `--emit cargo-project` already emits
the project and cannot be combined with `--keep-project`.
